{#- Shared content for every individual plan page (ES/EN/PT). Included by the
    three thin pagination shells: site/planes/p/plan.njk, site/en/plans/p/plan.njk,
    site/pt/planos/p/plan.njk — each just sets `lang` and paginates a different
    slice of plans.byLanguage. `plan` comes from the pagination alias.

    Standing decisions this implements (growth-roadmap.md storefront section):
    Option A (redirect to TP, no checkout) · email capture before the redirect,
    non-blocking · redirect carries UTM + plan_id · All-Access promo module ·
    Product schema. -#}
{%- set u = planUi[lang] -%}
{%- set aa = allAccess[lang] -%}
{%- set home = site.languages[lang].home -%}
{%- set plansUrl = { es: "/planes/", en: "/en/plans/", pt: "/pt/planos/" }[lang] -%}
{%- set sportLabel = u.sport[plan.sport] or plan.sport -%}
{%- set difficultyLabel = u.difficulty[plan.difficulty] -%}
{%- set metricLabel = u.metric[plan.metric] -%}
{%- set buyUrl = plan.url | withUtm(plan.id) -%}

<section class="plan-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="{{ home }}">{{ u.breadcrumbHome }}</a> / <a href="{{ plansUrl }}">{{ u.breadcrumbPlans }}</a> / {{ plan.displayName }}</p>
    <span class="label">{{ sportLabel }}{% if plan.distance %} · {{ plan.distance }}{% endif %}</span>
    <h1>{{ plan.displayName }}</h1>
    {#- Chips, September 10, 2026. The facts a buyer screens on — duration,
        level, metric, hours per week — were spread across a meta line, a flag
        row and a spec list further down. One row, one read. Hours/week is the
        one most people decide on and it was the furthest away.
        ⚠️ The class is `.plan-chip`, NOT the bare `.chip` this markup wants to
        be called: `.chip` is defined only in `members-carrera.css` and
        `admin-secuencias.css`, neither of which a plan page loads, so the bare
        name would have rendered unstyled text on 328 pages with a clean build
        and a green suite. Same family as `.aa-shot` below. -#}
    <div class="plan-chips">
      {%- if plan.weeks %}<span class="plan-chip">{{ plan.weeks }} {{ u.weeksLabel }}</span>{% endif %}
      {%- if difficultyLabel %}<span class="plan-chip">{{ difficultyLabel }}</span>{% endif %}
      {%- if metricLabel %}<span class="plan-chip">{{ metricLabel }}</span>{% endif %}
      {%- if plan.weeklyTotals and plan.weeklyTotals.hoursText %}<span class="plan-chip">{{ plan.weeklyTotals.hoursText }}{{ u.perWeekShort }}</span>{% endif %}
      {%- if plan.strength %}<span class="plan-chip plan-chip--flag">{{ u.strengthFlag }}</span>{% endif %}
      {%- if plan.weightLoss %}<span class="plan-chip plan-chip--flag">{{ u.weightLossFlag }}</span>{% endif %}
      {%- if plan.timeGoal %}<span class="plan-chip plan-chip--flag">{{ u.timeGoalFlag }}</span>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    THE OFFER BLOCK. Rebuilt September 10, 2026 on Iván's read of the live page,
    against an external audit.

    🚨 The rule this block now obeys: **one price and one primary action in the
    first screen.** What shipped that morning put this plan's price beside
    All-Access's, which asks the reader to pick a commercial model before they
    have decided the plan is theirs. All-Access survives here as ONE LINE under
    the button; the card itself moved below "Para quién es este plan", where a
    reader who has decided meets the alternative. `monthly-close/2026-08.md` is
    why the trade is cheap: All-Access went 3 → 1 subscriber, NRR 27.3%, and the
    remaining subscriber has never logged in — its problem is delivery, not
    exposure, so the first screen was being spent on a product that converts
    nobody.

    Left column is the WEEK, which is the object a buyer actually screens on and
    which this page has never shown as anything but a table row.
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -#}
<section class="plan-offer">
  <div class="wrap plan-offer-grid{% if not plan.weeklyBreakdown %} plan-offer-grid--solo{% endif %}">

    {%- if plan.weeklyBreakdown %}
    <div class="plan-week">
      <h2>{{ u.weekTitle }}</h2>
      <p class="plan-week-intro">{{ u.weekIntro }}</p>
      {#- Stat blocks, not a table. Same data the breakdown table carried — this
          REPLACES it rather than joining it, because the page was stating
          sessions-per-week twice (a spec list in the buy box and again in the
          table) and neither was the thing you look at.
          ⚠️ A seven-day grid is NOT derivable and was deliberately not built:
          the session counts sum to exactly 7 on only 145 of the 301 plans that
          have breakdown data — doubles push 62 of them to 8 and 33 to 9 — so a
          weekday calendar would be wrong on half the catalogue. What is honest
          is the SHAPE of the week: how many of each, how long, and how long the
          longest one is. -#}
      <div class="plan-week-grid">
        {%- for a in plan.weeklyBreakdown.activities %}
        <div class="plan-week-block">
          <span class="plan-week-n">{{ a.weeklyCount or "—" }}</span>
          <span class="plan-week-label">{{ u.activity[a.type] or a.type }}</span>
          <span class="plan-week-unit">{% if a.weeklyCount == 1 %}{{ u.unitSession }}{% else %}{{ u.unitSessions }}{% endif %}</span>
          {%- if a.weeklyAvg %}
          <span class="plan-week-detail">{{ a.weeklyAvg | formatWeeklyStat(a.weeklyAvgUnit) }}{{ u.perWeekShort }}</span>
          {%- endif %}
          {#- Heat on the longest session, and nowhere else on this page.
              `brand-guidelines.md` §3.3: Heat marks "the hard end of something",
              and the longest session is the hard end of the week — it is also
              the single figure that decides whether a plan fits someone's
              Sunday. If that justification stops being true, the colour goes,
              not the figure. -#}
          {%- if a.longest %}
          <span class="plan-week-longest">{{ u.longestShort }} <b>{{ a.longest | formatWeeklyStat(a.longestUnit) }}</b></span>
          {%- endif %}
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- if plan.weeklyBreakdown.restDaysPerWeek %}
        <div class="plan-week-block plan-week-block--rest">
          <span class="plan-week-n">{{ plan.weeklyBreakdown.restDaysPerWeek }}</span>
          <span class="plan-week-label">{{ u.weekRestLabel }}</span>
          <span class="plan-week-unit">{% if plan.weeklyBreakdown.restDaysPerWeek == 1 %}{{ u.unitDay }}{% else %}{{ u.unitDays }}{% endif %}</span>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}

    {#- The rail: the one action on this page. It is NOT sticky — that was tried
        and measured away; see the note on `.plan-rail-inner` in plan-page.css. -#}
    <aside class="plan-rail">
      <div class="plan-rail-inner">
        <div class="plan-buy-price">US$ {{ plan.price }} <span>{{ u.priceOnceSuffix }}</span></div>
        <a href="{{ buyUrl }}" class="btn-primary btn-buy plan-buy-btn plan-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ u.ctaBuy }}</a>
        <p class="plan-buy-note">{{ u.ctaNote }}</p>
        {#- All-Access, demoted to a sentence. It is a LINK, not a button:
            a second button here would be the same defect in smaller type. -#}
        <a class="plan-rail-aa" href="{{ aa.url }}">{{ u.aaInline | replace("{price}", aa.price) }}</a>
        {#- Credential line, Aug 27, 2026. One edit here reaches every plan page in
            all three languages — the largest indexed surface this site has. Copy is
            owned by _data/credentials.json, never written here. -#}
        <p class="plan-credential">{{ credentials[lang].planLine }} <a href="{{ credentials[lang].aboutHref }}">{{ credentials[lang].aboutLabel }}</a></p>
      </div>
    </aside>

  </div>
  {%- if not plan.weeklyBreakdown %}
  <div class="wrap"><p class="plan-nobreakdown">{{ u.noBreakdown }}</p></div>
  {%- endif %}
</section>

{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Generated content sections (August 6, 2026).

    Written from the plan's own data — inventory flags plus the weekly-breakdown
    crawl — rather than copied from the TrainingPeaks listing. The hand-written
    listing rewrites cover 20 of 321 plans, so copying them would leave 301
    pages empty; and reusing that text verbatim would set these pages against
    trainingpeaks.com for the same queries, which this domain loses. Every
    bullet below is conditional: a plan with no breakdown data simply renders
    fewer of them rather than asserting something unmeasured.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- -#}
{%- set totals = plan.weeklyTotals -%}
{%- set sib = plan.siblings -%}

<section class="plan-prose">
  <div class="wrap plan-prose-grid">

    <div class="plan-prose-block">
      <h2>{{ u.forWhoTitle }}</h2>
      <ul class="plan-list">
        {%- if u.forWhoLevel[plan.difficulty] %}<li>{{ u.forWhoLevel[plan.difficulty] }}</li>{% endif %}
        {%- if totals and totals.sessions %}
        <li>
          {%- if totals.hoursText -%}
            {{ u.forWhoTime | replace("{sessions}", totals.sessions) | replace("{hours}", totals.hoursText) }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ u.forWhoTimeNoHours | replace("{sessions}", totals.sessions) }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </li>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if totals and totals.longestText %}<li>{{ u.forWhoLongest | replace("{longest}", totals.longestText) }}</li>{% endif %}
        {%- if plan.weeks %}<li>{{ u.forWhoWeeks | replace("{weeks}", plan.weeks) }}</li>{% endif %}
        {%- if u.forWhoMetric[plan.metric] %}<li>{{ u.forWhoMetric[plan.metric] }}</li>{% endif %}
      </ul>
      {%- if sib and (sib.easier or sib.harder or sib.shorter or sib.longer) %}
      <p class="plan-siblings"><strong>{{ u.forWhoNotFit }}</strong>
        {%- if sib.easier %} <a href="{{ sib.easier.pageUrl }}">{{ u.siblingEasier | replace("{level}", u.difficulty[sib.easier.difficulty]) }}</a>{% endif %}
        {%- if sib.harder %} <a href="{{ sib.harder.pageUrl }}">{{ u.siblingHarder | replace("{level}", u.difficulty[sib.harder.difficulty]) }}</a>{% endif %}
        {%- if sib.shorter %} <a href="{{ sib.shorter.pageUrl }}">{{ u.siblingShorter | replace("{weeks}", sib.shorter.weeks) }}</a>{% endif %}
        {%- if sib.longer %} <a href="{{ sib.longer.pageUrl }}">{{ u.siblingLonger | replace("{weeks}", sib.longer.weeks) }}</a>{% endif %}
      </p>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="plan-prose-block">
      <h2>{{ u.methodTitle }}</h2>
      <ul class="plan-list">
        <li>{{ u.methodPolarized }}</li>
        <li>{{ u.methodProgression }}</li>
        {%- if plan.strength %}<li>{{ u.methodStrength }}</li>{% endif %}
        <li>{{ u.methodZones }}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>


  </div>
</section>

{#- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    ALL-ACCESS, in its new position: after the reader has met "para quién" and
    "cómo funciona", and before the practical half of the page. Moved here from
    the buy box September 10, 2026 (see the note on `.plan-offer`).

    It does two jobs at once, which is why it sits mid-page rather than at the
    foot. It is the alternative offer for someone who has now decided the plan
    is right — and it is the SEPARATOR. Iván's read of the live page: "the
    moment you scroll down, we are back to having 4 boxes of bullet points with
    no separator, no color in between, no nothing." A carbon band across the
    middle of that slab is the break, and it is a break made of product rather
    than of decoration.

    ⚠️ Carbon is permitted here by `brand-guidelines.md` §3.3 as the **featured
    offer card**, with that component's signature 3px Heat rule on the top edge
    and a Heat badge — a signal, never a button. The CTA is blue.
    **Do not restyle this toward the pink/navy of the TrainingPeaks card it is
    modelled on**: the structure is the borrowed part, the palette is ours.
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -#}
<section class="plan-aa-band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <aside class="plan-aa-card plan-aa-card--wide">
      <div class="plan-aa-main">
        <div class="plan-aa-head">
          <span class="plan-aa-badge">{{ u.aaCardBadge }}</span>
          <span class="plan-aa-price">US$ {{ aa.price }}<span>{{ u.allAccessPriceSuffix }}</span></span>
        </div>
        <h2>{{ u.aaCardHeading }}</h2>
        <ul class="plan-aa-list">
          {%- for line in u.aaCardBullets %}
          <li>{{ line }}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="plan-aa-side">
        <a href="{{ aa.url }}" class="btn-primary plan-aa-cta">{{ u.aaCardCta }}</a>
        <p class="plan-aa-compare">{{ u.aaCardCompare }}</p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="plan-prose plan-prose--practical">
  <div class="wrap plan-prose-grid">

    <div class="plan-prose-block">
      <h2>{{ u.gearTitle }}</h2>
      <ul class="plan-list">
        {%- if u.gearMetric[plan.metric] %}<li>{{ u.gearMetric[plan.metric] }}</li>{% endif %}
        {%- if u.gearSport[plan.sport] %}<li>{{ u.gearSport[plan.sport] }}</li>{% endif %}
        {%- if plan.strength %}<li>{{ u.gearStrength }}</li>{% endif %}
        <li>{{ u.gearTP }}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="plan-prose-block">
      <h2>{{ u.tpTitle }}</h2>
      <ul class="plan-list">
        <li>{{ u.tpSync }}</li>
        <li>{{ u.tpApp }}</li>
        <li>{{ u.tpStart }}</li>
        <li>{{ u.tpReusable }}</li>
        <li>{{ u.tpSupport }}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

{#- The one image on this page, September 10, 2026. It is a real TrainingPeaks
    calendar with a plan already applied — the thing the buyer is actually
    purchasing, which the page described in four bullets and never showed.

    🚨 It is NOT this plan's week, and the caption says so in every language.
    A screenshot of someone else's calendar presented as "your plan" is the one
    class of error on this page that would matter; labelling it as an example
    costs one sentence.

    ⚠️ The figure class is `.plan-shot`, not All-Access's `.aa-shot`. That
    component is defined in `all-access.css`, which plan pages do not load —
    reusing the name would have rendered an unstyled image on 328 pages and the
    build would not have complained. Fifth-and-sixth instance of the same defect
    family this branch keeps producing.

    srcset carries the same two widths All-Access proved: 2200 px for the 2×
    desktop case, 1600 px so a phone does not download the large one. -#}
<section class="plan-shot-section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>{{ u.tpShotTitle }}</h2>
    <figure class="plan-shot">
      <picture>
        <source type="image/webp" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 1032px"
                srcset='{{ "/assets/images/tp-calendario.webp" | v }} 1600w, {{ "/assets/images/tp-calendario-2200.webp" | v }} 2200w'>
        <img src="{{ "/assets/images/tp-calendario-2200.jpg" | v }}" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 1032px"
             srcset='{{ "/assets/images/tp-calendario.jpg" | v }} 1600w, {{ "/assets/images/tp-calendario-2200.jpg" | v }} 2200w'
             width="2200" height="1053" alt="{{ u.tpShotAlt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      </picture>
      <figcaption>{{ u.tpShotCaption }}</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

{#- "Not sure this is the right plan?" — the honest version of what the email
    capture was pretending to be. The old copy offered to email the plan, which
    isn't something we can actually do; this asks the question a hesitant buyer
    is already asking and gives two ways to ask it, one of them immediate.
    Placed after the content and before the buy CTA: by here the reader knows
    what the plan involves, so doubt is at its peak. Added Aug 6, 2026. -#}
{#- Two ways to ask, side by side on the same grid as the buy box above.
    The mailto link that used to sit here was the odd one out: the box above
    captured an address, this one handed the reader to their mail client and
    captured nothing, so an identical question produced a lead or didn't
    depending on which button they happened to press. Now both routes are
    instrumented — WhatsApp opens a pre-filled thread, the form creates the
    lead in Twenty. Same form component as the buy box, tagged `helpbox` so
    the two placements stay distinguishable in GA4 and in `leadNotes`. -#}
<section class="plan-help">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>{{ u.helpHeading }}</h2>
    <p class="plan-help-intro">{{ u.helpBody }}</p>
    <div class="plan-help-grid">
      <div class="plan-help-col">
        <a class="btn-whatsapp"
           href="{{ site.whatsapp }}?text={{ (u.waText | replace("{plan}", plan.displayName)) | urlencode }}"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ u.helpWhatsapp }}</a>
        <p class="plan-help-note">{{ u.helpNote }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="plan-help-col plan-capture">
        {% set captureSource = "helpbox" %}
        {% include "partials/plan-capture-form.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- Closing buy CTA moved above All-Access (Iván, Aug 6, 2026): the page should
    make its own offer last, not hand the reader to a different product on the
    way out. `.btn-primary` is white-on-blue by default — correct inside the
    dark `.cta-final`, wrong on a white section — so this one is explicitly
    reversed to blue-on-white via `.btn-buy`. -#}
<section class="plan-final-cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a href="{{ buyUrl }}" class="btn-primary btn-buy plan-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ u.ctaBuy }}</a>
    <p class="plan-buy-note">{{ u.ctaNote }}</p>
  </div>
</section>

{#- The foot All-Access module was REMOVED September 10, 2026. With the card
    now mid-page and a line in the buy rail, it was the third mention of the
    same product on one page, and the last thing a reader saw was a different
    product than the one the page sells. -#}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Product",
  "name": {{ plan.displayName | dump | safe }},
  {#- Schema description now carries the same measured facts the page shows —
      sessions per week and average weekly hours — instead of restating the
      title. More useful in a rich result, and still no duplicated TP copy. -#}
  "description": {{ (plan.weeks + " " + u.weeksLabel + " — " + sportLabel
      + (", " + plan.distance if plan.distance else "")
      + (", " + difficultyLabel if difficultyLabel else "")
      + (". " + (u.forWhoTimeNoHours | replace("{sessions}", totals.sessions)) if totals and totals.sessions and not totals.hoursText else "")
      + (". " + (u.forWhoTime | replace("{sessions}", totals.sessions) | replace("{hours}", totals.hoursText)) if totals and totals.sessions and totals.hoursText else "")
      ) | dump | safe }},
  "image": {{ site.defaultProductImage | absoluteUrl | dump | safe }},
  "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": "Triaperformance" },
  "offers": {
    "@type": "Offer",
    "url": {{ plan.url | dump | safe }},
    "priceCurrency": "USD",
    "price": {{ plan.price | dump | safe }},
    "availability": "https://schema.org/InStock"
  }
}
</script>
<script src="{{ "/assets/js/plan-capture.js" | v }}" defer></script>
